# the argument of hobbes-leviathan-1.md as claude-opus-5-5 read it: check that it says what the text says
logic	kd
atom	def_evident	in the definition of civil law there is nothing that is not at first sight evident
atom	laws_to_addressed	laws are laws to every one of those to whom the command is directed, and to none else
atom	rules_just	laws are the rules of just and unjust
atom	unjust_contrary_law	nothing is reputed unjust that is not contrary to some law
atom	only_cw_makes	none can make laws but the commonwealth
atom	subjection_cw	our subjection is to the commonwealth only
atom	signs_required	commands are to be signified by sufficient signs
atom	no_other_way_obey	a man knows not otherwise how to obey commands than by sufficient signs
atom	ack_deduced	whatsoever can by necessary consequence be deduced from the definition is acknowledged for truth
# "can make" in S4 is read as an atom (no one has the authority to make laws), not as a modal possibility
# "are to be signified" in S4 is kept inside the atom signs_required rather than written with ought
